# A ball with a one-limb center times a number a of the format: |xa - cx a| <= |a| rx, plus the
# error of the rounded center product, at most U |cz| + V from the claims of mul_1_1.
kernel:        ball_scale_1
input:         cx
input:         rx
input:         a
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         cx*a
requires:      nonneg rx
ensures:       encloses cz rz x*a x=cx,rx
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_scale_1_correct
source:        midpoint-radius scaling (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

cz = prod(cx, a)
aa = abs(a)
t1 = rmul(aa, rx)
mz = abs(cz)
d0 = rmul(const unit_computed(mul_1_1), mz)
d  = radd(d0, const tiny_computed(mul_1_1))
rz = radd(t1, d)
